  model: claude-opus-5
  left-out: The "History" section has no prose of its own in the source, only a
    map figure; its body here is a single bridging sentence assembled from
    claims made in its subsections, and the map is placed there in the image
    plan. Several pictures in the article are not among the supplied file
    names — the panoramic view of the theatre, the Didyma temple and Apollo
    statue in "Ties with Megara", the electrum and silver coinage, the vase
    fragments in "Examples of the Milesian Vase" and the eight gallery
    photographs — so they have no image-plan entries; "Gallery" and "Examples
    of the Milesian Vase" are kept as their original captions and the one line
    of prose the latter carries. "Second Achaemenid period", "Roman period",
    "Fall of Miletus", "Late Bronze Age", "Middle Bronze Age", "Archaic
    period" and "Geography" carry no footnote references in the source, so
    none could be carried into the rewrite. The list sections ("Colonies",
    "Notable people", "References and sources") are reproduced as lists rather
    than turned into prose.
