[[ ^9 ]]: The late fantasy fiction of [[ Antoninus Liberalis ]], //Metamorphoses// XXX 1–2 after Nicander, can be safely disregarded as being in any way history. His entertaining tales have the imaginary character named [[ Miletus | miletus-hero ]] fleeing [[ Crete ]] to avoid being forced to become the [[ eromenos ]] of King [[ Minos ]]. He founds the city only after slaying a giant named Asterius, son of [[ Anax | anax-mythology ]], after whom the region known as Miletus was called 'Anactoria', "place of Anax". [[ Anax ]] in Greek means "the king" and [[ Asterius | asterius-mythology ]] is "starry".

